    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Membership Inference over <span class="search-hit mathjax">Diffusion</span>-<span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span>-based Synthetic Tabular Data
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Cheng%2C+P">Peini Cheng</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Bahmani%2C+A">Amir Bahmani</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.16037v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        This study investigates the privacy risks associated with <span class="search-hit mathjax">diffusion</span>-based synthetic tabular data generation methods, focusing on their susceptibility to Membership Inference Attacks (MIAs). We examine two recent&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.16037v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2510.16037v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.16037v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        This study investigates the privacy risks associated with <span class="search-hit mathjax">diffusion</span>-based synthetic tabular data generation methods, focusing on their susceptibility to Membership Inference Attacks (MIAs). We examine two recent <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span>, TabDDPM and TabSyn, by developing query-based MIAs based on the step-wise error comparison method. Our findings reveal that TabDDPM is more vulnerable to these attacks. TabSyn exhibits resilience against our attack <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span>. Our work underscores the importance of evaluating the privacy implications of <span class="search-hit mathjax">diffusion</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span> and encourages further research into robust privacy-preserving mechanisms for synthetic data generation.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.16037v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2510.16037v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

